    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties. This was an upfront-quoted trip (fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 34.50 on EV-FARE-00115), which decides most of the case.\n\nTHE DISTANCE CLAIM. The rider is right on the facts and wrong on the money. On the governing trace figure (EV-GPS-00115, trace_distance_km 28.18, not the rounded 28.2 on the trip record) the car covered 5.78 km / 25.8% more than the 22.4 km booked optimal, so a deviation IS established under POL-RD-01 (both gates, 20% and 0.8 km, pass). It is not a MATERIAL deviation (needs 50% or 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check was not required on materiality; I ran it anyway and there is no pattern — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against completed_trips_90d 523 (0.19%), far below 3 flags or 5%. But under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges on an upfront-quoted trip were fixed at $34.50 at booking, POL-RD-02 does not run, and the rider cannot recover for the extra distance however large the excess is. The driver's attempt to be paid for the detour also fails: POL-RD-04 needs a rider instruction naming a place or road, and the only route message is the driver's own at 21:14:10 ('CTE very heavy boss, i go KPE then TPE'), acknowledged by the rider with 'ok' and a null waypoint_hint. POL-RD-03 fails too — EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, no advisory covers CTE/KPE/TPE in the window), so there is no advisory, no validity window and no shortest_lawful_alternative_km, and a bare 'traffic was heavy' does not discharge the driver's burden under POL-RD-08.\n\nTHE MONEY. Charged total was $39.00 against the $34.50 quote — a gap of $4.50, and that gap is exactly the two ERP lines (EV-FARE-00115). One of them stands: KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) at $2.50, on the optimal route, with the trace passing within 44.5 m at 21:32:40, inside the 250 m crossing radius, so it is properly chargeable. The other does not: 'AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas)' at $2.00, not on the optimal route, and the closest the trace ever comes to that gantry is 5,419 m — sixteen times the match radius. That is a phantom billing line, refunded in full as a standalone correction under POL-RD-09(4), which is available whether or not a deviation exists. Refund = charged_total 39.00 − quoted_fare 34.50 − properly chargeable KPE pass 2.50 − waiting_time_fee 0.00 = $2.00. The rider's own reconciliation reaches the same $2.00.\n\nNO ESCALATION AND NO CONDUCT REFERRAL. The trace is unimpaired (100% coverage, 229 fixes, 10 s interval, maximum gap 0 s), so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) do not fire; trip identifiers and timestamps agree across the artifacts, so POL-RD-10(2) and (4) do not fire; and the only unmatched fare line is the one refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excepts. POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct review is not engaged because no repeat pattern exists and the deviation is not material. All of these artifacts carry weight 1.0, so nothing is discounted and nothing is held.\n\nRESULT. PARTIAL_REFUND of $2.00 to the rider; the rest of the charge stands. A billing-integrity referral on the phantom AYE line is recorded above."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

